cameraserver: do not start at boot on the MT8163 Echo Show devices

The ROM built from this repository ships the complete MediaTek camera
stack: 45 proprietary blobs, the passthrough provider, the compatibility
shim and the private display framework. None of it can work until two more
pieces are installed on the device itself - the cmdq event-id shim, which
has to be built against the device's own bionic, and camera-bringup.rc,
which grants the ISP its M4U/SMI permissions and mounts /persist.

Between flashing the ROM and installing those, any client that opens the
camera sends the HAL into an endless retry: ISP_WaitIrq times out on
PASS1_TG1_DON, the ioctl fails, the sensor is powered down and back up,
roughly every 0.6 s, indefinitely. Captured from the console of such a
boot:

    ISP_WaitIrq ERROR: ...WaitStatus(0x00000400),Timeout(500)
    ISP_ioctl ERROR: Fail, Cmd(1074817798), (process)=(PreviewCmdQueTh,...)
    [PowerDown]pinSetIdx:0, currSensorName: ov02b10_mipi_raw
    [PowerON]pinSetIdx:0, currSensorName: ov02b10_mipi_raw

That is enough to leave the device unresponsive with a lit but black
screen: adbd still answers, but no new process can be spawned, and only a
power cycle recovers it. It needs no user action to trigger - a kiosk or
security app that opens the camera at startup is sufficient.

Starting cameraserver disabled closes that window. It is a one-line
change, and scripts/install-cmdq-event-shim.sh already removes the line
once the shim is in place, so the camera comes up normally from the next
boot onward.

Apply from the source tree root:
    patch -p1 < 0013-cameraserver-do-not-start-until-shim-installed.patch

diff --git a/frameworks/av/camera/cameraserver/cameraserver.rc b/frameworks/av/camera/cameraserver/cameraserver.rc
index 8f51458..ba0c76d 100644
--- a/frameworks/av/camera/cameraserver/cameraserver.rc
+++ b/frameworks/av/camera/cameraserver/cameraserver.rc
@@ -1,5 +1,14 @@
 service cameraserver /system/bin/cameraserver
     class main
+    # Not started at boot on the MT8163 Echo Show devices. The ROM ships the
+    # full MediaTek camera stack, but it cannot work until the cmdq event
+    # shim and camera-bringup.rc are installed on the device, and a camera
+    # client that opens it before then retries forever - ISP IRQ timeout,
+    # sensor power-down, power-up, ~0.6 s per cycle - until the whole device
+    # is unresponsive with a lit but black screen.
+    # scripts/install-cmdq-event-shim.sh removes this line once the shim is
+    # in place.
+    disabled
     user cameraserver
     group audio camera input drmrpc
     ioprio rt 4
